  "steps": [
    "Whisk the sauce ingredients in a small bowl until the cornstarch dissolves.",
    "Bring a pot of water to a boil. Blanch the noodles 20-30 sec until they loosen, then drain well. Do not rinse.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp of the oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat. Stir-fry the cabbage, celery and onion about 1 min, until they start to soften.",
    "Push the vegetables aside and add the remaining oil. Add the noodles, re-whisk the sauce, and pour it in. Toss 1-2 min until the sauce thickens and every strand is coated."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "4 servings, about 390 cal each.",
    "Look for fresh chow mein or yakisoba noodles in the refrigerated case at an Asian grocery; fresh ramen also works."
